Overlay patch 0040: the VR enhancement-CVar stash (VR-spec D9,
VR-DONOR-MAP §5b).

Pre-rendered 2D backdrops and fixed cameras are unusable in stereo -- they are
a flat painting where the world should be, and a camera that refuses to follow
the head. The donor ships both of SoH's existing replacement enhancements
defaulted ON in VR. We ship only the 3DSceneRender half on by default --
DisableFixedCamera is gated behind gSohIos.VrDisableFixedCamera (default 0)
after R1 took a SIGSEGV inside Camera_Normal1 with it forced on; see the
in-patch comment for the reasoning. We do NOT flip the shipped defaults (that would change the
flat and 3D-panel builds); the shell asks for the override on VR entry and
gives it back on exit. Because these enhancements install their hooks through
RegisterShipInitFunc, setting the CVar is not enough -- ShipInit::Init must be
re-run for that path, which is what SohIos_VRApplyEnhancementCVars does.

CRASH-SAFE RESTORE (spec D9): iOS swipe-kill is SIGKILL, so a VR session
that dies mid-flight would otherwise leave the user's flat game permanently
overridden. The pre-VR values are stashed into gSohIos.VrStash.* and saved
synchronously BEFORE the override; SohIos_VRRestoreStashedCVars() runs on boot,
before the enhancements register, and puts them back if the stash is still
armed.

The VR sim-rate override that used to live here moved into overlay 0015 rev3:
it has to sit at the very top of GetInterpolationFPS, ahead of 0015's own
MatchRefreshRate cap, and a second patch inserting into text 0015 owns breaks
0015's reverse probe in apply-overlay.sh. Same "regenerate, do not stack"
rule 0031 records.

rev2 (VR R2a, device round): 3DSceneRender NO LONGER DEFAULTS ON IN VR.
R1 kept the donor's default-on for it on the grounds that it is "the
stereo-critical one". The first headset build proved that backwards: SoH's own
tooltip is "Enable this when using a mod that implements 3D backdrops for these
areas", and with no such mod installed the enhancement draws the room's bare
placeholder mesh -- the user's Link's house came back an all-green box. His
Documents/mods holds a 4K TEXTURE pack, which is not that mod, and the donor
ships no such mod either (its own SohMenuEnhancements.cpp just sets
DefaultValue(true) on the same checkbox and keeps the same tooltip).
So the enhancement is now driven by the shell's THREE-WAY room setting,
gSohVRRoomMode -- 0 panel (default, overlay 0039 rev2 routes image-backed rooms
to the world-locked panel), 1 flat, 2 3d -- and only mode 2 forces it on. The
CVar stays fully available to the user in the enhancements menu; VR simply
stops overriding it. The stash machinery is untouched and still crash-safe.

This block is anchored ABOVE OTRGlobals::HasOriginal() precisely to stay clear
of 0015's hunks. __IOS__-only.

--- a/soh/soh/OTRGlobals.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/OTRGlobals.cpp
@@ -995,7 +995,135 @@
 bool OTRGlobals::HasMasterQuest() {
     return hasMasterQuest;
 }
+
+#ifdef __IOS__
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0040, VR-spec D9 / VR-DONOR-MAP 5b): the enhancement
+// CVars VR overrides, with a crash-safe stash. Anchored above HasOriginal() to
+// stay clear of overlay 0015's hunks in GetInterpolationFPS just below.
+// The two enhancements VR overrides (VR-DONOR-MAP 5b). Kept as a table so the
+// stash, the override and the restore can never drift apart.
+static const char* const kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[] = {
+    CVAR_ENHANCEMENT("3DSceneRender"),      // pre-rendered 2D backdrops -> 3D
+    CVAR_ENHANCEMENT("DisableFixedCamera"), // fixed cameras -> follow the player
+};
+static const char* const kSohIosVrStashCVars[] = {
+    "gSohIos.VrStash.3DSceneRender",
+    "gSohIos.VrStash.DisableFixedCamera",
+};
+// Which of them VR actually forces, and the default for each.
+//
+// DisableFixedCamera defaults OFF, against the donor. R1 took a SIGSEGV in
+// Camera_Normal1 (NULL deref at +0x7f2, called from Camera_Update) during the
+// Kokiri intro with it forced on, and it is the only thing in the VR change
+// set that mutates camera state at runtime: its OnCameraState hook calls
+// Camera_ChangeSetting(CAM_SET_NORMAL0) + Camera_ChangeMode(CAM_MODE_NORMAL)
+// on the main camera, which reaches Camera_Normal1 in scenes that never
+// expected it. Causation is strongly indicated but not isolated, and a crash
+// nobody has reproduced deliberately is not something to ship into a headset,
+// so VR leaves the user's own setting alone until R2 proves or fixes it.
+// 3DSceneRender is the stereo-critical one (a flat painted backdrop where the
+// world should be) and keeps the donor's default-on.
+// rev3 (VR R2b): DisableFixedCamera is now forced OFF in room mode 0 -- see
+// SohIos_VRDesiredEnhancement below for why the green floor made that
+// necessary. The R1 SIGSEGV gate still governs modes 1 and 2.
+static const char* const kSohIosVrGateCVars[] = {
+    "gSohIos.VrScene3D", // rev2: superseded by gSohVRRoomMode, kept for the table's shape
+    "gSohIos.VrDisableFixedCamera",
+};
+static const int kSohIosVrGateDefaults[] = { 0, 0 };
+#define SOHIOS_VR_ENHANCEMENT_COUNT \
+    ((int)(sizeof(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars) / sizeof(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[0])))
 
+// rev2: how VR treats a pre-rendered (image-backed) room -- 0 panel (default),
+// 1 flat, 2 3d. Owned by the shell (SohIosShell.m), read here and by overlay
+// 0039 rev2's flat-screen latch, so the two can never disagree about which
+// treatment is in force.
+extern "C" volatile int gSohVRRoomMode;
+
+// Does VR want to force enhancement `idx` on?
+//   idx 0, 3DSceneRender: ONLY in room mode 2 ("3d"), which is the mode that
+//     says "I have installed a 3D-backdrop mod". In every other mode the
+//     enhancement would replace authored 2D art with a placeholder mesh.
+//   idx 1, DisableFixedCamera: the R1 SIGSEGV gate, unchanged.
+// rev3 (VR R2b): the answer is a VALUE, not a boolean -- -1 means "leave the
+// user's own setting alone", 0 and 1 mean "force it there for the session".
+//   idx 0, 3DSceneRender: forced ON only in room mode 2 ("3d"), which is the
+//     mode that says "I have installed a 3D-backdrop mod". Otherwise untouched.
+//   idx 1, DisableFixedCamera: forced OFF in room mode 0, the shipped default.
+//     Reason, from the user's 1.0.1.2 screenshot of Link's house: z_room.c draws
+//     the authored pre-rendered background ONLY when the active camera is
+//     CAM_SET_PREREND_FIXED (func_80096680, the `sp9C` test) -- and it draws
+//     the room's own polygonDlist->opa geometry underneath it either way. This
+//     enhancement's OnCameraState hook changes the setting to CAM_SET_NORMAL0,
+//     so the background never draws and what shows instead is that bare
+//     geometry, whose floor in Link's house is an untextured GREEN quad. Room
+//     mode 0 exists to present the art AS AUTHORED on the panel, so it cannot
+//     also be disabling the camera the art was authored for. Modes 1 and 2 keep
+//     the R1 gate (the user's own gSohIos.VrDisableFixedCamera opt-in, still
+//     default-off behind the R1 Camera_Normal1 SIGSEGV).
+static int SohIos_VRDesiredEnhancement(int idx) {
+    if (idx == 0) {
+        return (gSohVRRoomMode == 2) ? 1 : -1;
+    }
+    if (gSohVRRoomMode == 0) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return (CVarGetInteger(kSohIosVrGateCVars[idx], kSohIosVrGateDefaults[idx]) != 0) ? 1 : -1;
+}
+
+// Restore anything a previous session left overridden (SIGKILL in VR). Runs
+// on boot, before the enhancements register their hooks.
+extern "C" void SohIos_VRRestoreStashedCVars(void) {
+    if (CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.VrStash.Active", 0) == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    for (int sohI = 0; sohI < SOHIOS_VR_ENHANCEMENT_COUNT; sohI++) {
+        CVarSetInteger(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI], CVarGetInteger(kSohIosVrStashCVars[sohI], 0));
+        CVarClear(kSohIosVrStashCVars[sohI]);
+    }
+    CVarClear("gSohIos.VrStash.Active");
+    CVarSave();
+    SPDLOG_INFO("SOH_IOS VR: restored enhancement CVars stashed by a previous session");
+}
+
+// on=1: stash + override + re-register. on=0: restore + re-register.
+// MAIN THREAD ONLY (it re-runs ShipInit hooks and writes the config).
+extern "C" void SohIos_VRApplyEnhancementCVars(int on) {
+    if (on) {
+        if (CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.VrStash.Active", 0) != 0) {
+            return; // already overridden (idempotent entry)
+        }
+        for (int sohI = 0; sohI < SOHIOS_VR_ENHANCEMENT_COUNT; sohI++) {
+            CVarSetInteger(kSohIosVrStashCVars[sohI], CVarGetInteger(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI], 0));
+        }
+        CVarSetInteger("gSohIos.VrStash.Active", 1);
+        CVarSave(); // the stash must survive a SIGKILL taken one line later
+        for (int sohI = 0; sohI < SOHIOS_VR_ENHANCEMENT_COUNT; sohI++) {
+            int sohWant = SohIos_VRDesiredEnhancement(sohI);
+            if (sohWant < 0) {
+                continue; // VR has no opinion: the user's own setting stands
+            }
+            if (CVarGetInteger(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI], 0) == sohWant) {
+                continue; // already there; no need to re-run the hooks
+            }
+            CVarSetInteger(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI], sohWant);
+            ShipInit::Init(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI]);
+        }
+    } else {
+        if (CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.VrStash.Active", 0) == 0) {
+            return; // nothing stashed (idempotent exit)
+        }
+        for (int sohI = 0; sohI < SOHIOS_VR_ENHANCEMENT_COUNT; sohI++) {
+            CVarSetInteger(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI], CVarGetInteger(kSohIosVrStashCVars[sohI], 0));
+            CVarClear(kSohIosVrStashCVars[sohI]);
+            ShipInit::Init(kSohIosVrEnhancementCVars[sohI]);
+        }
+        CVarClear("gSohIos.VrStash.Active");
+        CVarSave();
+    }
+}
+#endif
+
 bool OTRGlobals::HasOriginal() {
     return hasOriginal;
 }
@@ -1590,6 +1718,11 @@
     if (CVarGetInteger(CVAR_REMOTE_ANCHOR("Enabled"), 0)) {
         Anchor::Instance->Enable();
     }
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0040): put back anything a VR session that was
+    // SIGKILLed left overridden, BEFORE the enhancements register.
+    SohIos_VRRestoreStashedCVars();
+#endif
     ShipInit::InitAll();
     Rando::StaticData::InitHashMaps();
     OTRGlobals::Instance->gRandoContext->AddExcludedOptions();
